  "name": "Furizon",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Furizon is an Italian furry event and the non-profit association behind it, A.P.S. Furizon, held annually in northern Italy since 2015. The group was established in late 2014 by Silverwolf and Rigel, and in 2018 it became a legally certified non-profit association with an elected board. Furizon began as a self-managed furmeet in a location surrounded by nature, with themed group games, DJ sets and cooking contests, and in 2022 it held its first full hotel convention in Cavalese, Trentino, with panels, a dealers' den, live DJ sets, a fursuit lounge and an artist alley. The association also runs a spin-off convention called Riverside. Attendance has grown from 31 in 2015 to nearly 500 in 2026.",
